{"id": "EUVD-2026-59244", "enisaUuid": "26244734-29ad-3ef7-a5b0-7b3debbc722b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: LAG, Fix off-by-one in single-FDB error rollback\n\nOn failure at index i, the reverse cleanup loop in\nmlx5_lag_create_single_fdb() starts from i, so the failed index\nitself is rolled back. That can operate on uninitialized state or\ndouble-tear-down a rule the add_one path already self-rolled-back.\n\nStart the rollback from i - 1 so only successfully-installed entries\nare undone.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:19", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0be672071d6e8c4d3be6a8f796d8e47198763770", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40cc06bf71476932e5d139fa326dcd0372766e16", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f0e4ae6975c773f7854fc48932a267f6c79088f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72345", "GHSA-2cj4-xv36-4974"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "29c2195c-c714-3d9b-a6a8-fb522be75724", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.113 <6.13"}, {"id": "3d825f9c-8384-341f-83f6-ac7ed9ed4585", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "771e1daa-f787-3729-9f94-cc0378821229", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "7ec19b22-5785-3bb5-aba3-1359eb60a9ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddbb5ddc43ad000a984149db5af1133433938404 <40cc06bf71476932e5d139fa326dcd0372766e16"}, {"id": "8d5ae4d3-629a-362a-ac67-2f736e2ba6e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "95779045-6c7a-32c5-9cf0-cc0b11b93f63", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_versi